CAT = 'sgm9Law'; SEG = 'LAW'
Q = [
("In a life insurance contract, the insurer usually accepts the proposer's offer by:",
 'Issuing the policy', ['Receiving the proposal form', 'Sending a product summary', 'Arranging a medical exam'],
 'The proposal is the offer; the insurer accepts by issuing the policy on the terms proposed. Issuing on different terms is a counter-offer.'),
('A proposer lacks the mental capacity to understand the contract. Which essential element of a valid contract is missing?',
 'Capacity', ['Consideration', 'Offer', 'Legality'],
 'A valid contract needs offer, acceptance, consideration, legality and capacity. A party who cannot understand the contract lacks capacity.'),
("Under the LIA Code, a proposer's health changes after the proposal is signed. The proposer must tell the insurer if it happens before:",
 'The application is accepted', ['The proposal is signed', 'The first claim is made', 'The policy matures'],
 'The duty of disclosure runs until the contract is concluded, so any change in health before acceptance must be reported without delay.'),
("A woman insures her husband's life and they later divorce. The policy stays valid because insurable interest is needed only:",
 'At inception', ['At the time of claim', 'Throughout the term', 'At each renewal'],
 'For life insurance the interest must exist when the policy is taken out. Later loss of the relationship does not end the policy.'),
("A person's insurable interest in their own life is:",
 'Unlimited', ['Capped at their income', 'Capped at their debts', 'Nil'],
 "A person may insure their own life for any amount the insurer will accept, as the law presumes an unlimited interest in one's own life."),
('Because a life policy is not a contract of indemnity, a person may:',
 'Claim on several policies in full', ['Claim only the proven financial loss', 'Insure only up to annual income', 'Hold only one policy at a time'],
 'Life policies pay agreed sums, not a measured loss, so each policy pays its benefit even if the person holds policies with several insurers.'),
('An unclear term in a policy drafted by the insurer is usually read:',
 'Against the insurer', ["In the insurer's favour", 'As void in every case', 'By MAS for both parties'],
 'Because the insurer drafts the policy and the buyer cannot negotiate it, courts resolve any ambiguity against the insurer that wrote it.'),
('A proposer misstates a material fact and the insurer finds out. The contract is generally:',
 "Voidable at the insurer's option", ['Void from the start', 'Valid with no remedy', 'Converted to term cover'],
 'Misrepresentation of a material fact lets the innocent party, the insurer, choose to avoid the contract or let it stand.'),
('A fact is material if a prudent insurer would weigh it in setting:',
 'Its terms or the premium', ["The agent's commission", "The client's tax relief", 'The CPF interest rate'],
 'A material fact is one that would influence a prudent insurer in deciding whether to accept the risk and on what terms and premium.'),
("An insurer's conduct leads a client to reasonably believe its agent may collect premiums, though no such power was given. This is:",
 'Apparent authority', ['Express authority', 'Implied authority', 'Agency by necessity'],
 "Apparent (ostensible) authority arises from the principal's words or conduct towards the third party, and binds the principal."),
("Once a principal ratifies an agent's unauthorised act, the principal is bound:",
 'As if authority existed at the time', ['Only from the date it ratifies', "Only for the agent's later acts", 'Only if MAS gives consent'],
 'Ratification relates back: the act is treated as authorised from the moment it was done.'),
("An agent takes a hidden payment from a third party in a deal for the principal. This breaches the agent's duty:",
 'Not to make a secret profit', ['To act in person', 'To obey lawful instructions', 'To keep proper accounts for the principal'],
 "An agent must not profit from the agency without the principal's knowledge. A secret profit must be handed to the principal."),
('Which is a duty the principal owes the agent?',
 'To pay the agreed commission', ['To act with skill and care', "To keep the principal's secrets", 'To avoid conflicts of interest'],
 'The principal must pay the agreed remuneration and indemnify the agent for proper expenses. The other duties listed are owed by the agent.'),
("A client tells the insurer's agent about a health condition while the agent acts within authority. The law generally treats this as:",
 'Known to the insurer', ['Known to the agent', 'Not disclosed at all', 'Disclosed to MAS'],
 'Knowledge an agent gains while acting within authority is generally imputed to the principal, the insurer.'),
('An agency relationship ends by operation of law when the principal:',
 'Is made bankrupt', ['Changes address', 'Hires a second agent', 'Lowers the commission'],
 'Agency ends by law on events such as the death, mental incapacity or bankruptcy of the principal, as well as by agreement or revocation.'),
("Authority that is not stated but is reasonably needed to carry out the agent's express duties is:",
 'Implied authority', ['Apparent authority', 'Ratified authority', 'Authority by estoppel'],
 'Implied authority covers what is reasonably incidental to the express authority, such as routine steps needed to do the task given.'),
]
